save('examples.html','Examples and feedback calibration','''<h1>Task and feedback examples</h1><p>Illustrative classroom examples. Adapt them to what the tool actually supports.</p>
<table><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Goal-based task</th><th>Evidence and protected scope</th></tr><tr><td>Batch renamer</td><td>Give the three selected props exactly one SM_ prefix.</td><td>Inspect all three names and the unchanged unselected light. Restore names before next round.</td></tr><tr><td>Placement tool</td><td>Arrange three selected props in a row with 200 cm between origins.</td><td>Inspect coordinates and verify the unselected prop is unchanged. Restore original transforms.</td></tr><tr><td>Material Setup practice</td><td>Assign one prepared surface to the sample crate at slot 0.</td><td>One instance, one component assignment. Parent graph and shared mesh unchanged in the stated operation. Reset practice data.</td></tr><tr><td>VFX Placement practice</td><td>Place Steam at the three supplied markers at scale 1.00.</td><td>Three new effects in the sample. Repeated markers rejected. This does not measure frame cost.</td></tr><tr><td>Paper tool concept</td><td>Show how you would choose the objects to process and check the result.</td><td>Record interpretation, hesitation and missing information. Mark execution untested.</td></tr></table>
<h2>Calibration example</h2><p><strong>Too vague:</strong> “The interface is confusing.”</p><p><strong>Observed:</strong> “I selected three props. The preview did not name the targets, so I asked the author whether the light would change.”</p><p><strong>Consequence:</strong> “I could not check the scope before committing.”</p><p><strong>Hypothesis:</strong> “A list of affected objects may help.”</p><p><strong>Retest:</strong> “Give a new reviewer the same three props and light. Before Apply, ask them to identify every affected object from the preview. Record whether help is needed and check all four objects afterward.”</p>
<h2>A successful attempt is useful evidence</h2><p>“The preview listed the three selected props. I checked the names and completed the task without help. Keep that preview. No failure appeared in this attempt. Next test: empty selection should create no changes and explain the next action.” Mark that next test <strong>proposed</strong>.</p>
<h2>Conflicting reviews</h2><p>If one tester succeeds and another needs help, keep both observations. Compare the version, start state, domain familiarity and assistance. Choose a retest that isolates the uncertainty. Do not average these into a numeric grade.</p>''')
save('demo.html','Instructor demo run sheet','''<h1>My tool demo: Material & VFX Tools</h1><p><strong>Default classroom route:</strong> the current Stage 3 practice interface. Material Setup gets seven minutes at elapsed 19–26 (3:49–3:56 PM). After the existing two-minute interface/host explanation, VFX and recovery get four minutes at elapsed 28–32 (3:58–4:02 PM).</p>
<p>Keep the existing Maya/Unreal handoff in its separate seven-minute block. It still requires the instructor’s live rehearsal. This pack does not claim that bridge or the material/VFX Unreal adapter has been rehearsed.</p>
<h2>Preflight on the teaching machine</h2><ol><li>Open the Week07UnrealPython project. From its folder run <code>./.venv/Scripts/python.exe Scripts/assistants.py --stage 3</code>, or use the existing VS Code offline assistants task.</li><li>Confirm PRACTICE MODE. Start fresh with Prepared surface, MI_Crate_Demo, slot 0 and Steam at scale 1.00. The sample supplies selection. Clicking in Unreal does not change it.</li><li>Check projector readability and manually try Preview, Apply, duplicate rejection and Reset. Reset affects both sample workflows and retains input fields.</li><li>Have the linked captures open before class. If launch takes more than 30 seconds, use these actual recorded UI states and describe them as captures.</li></ol>
<h2>Seven-minute material demonstration</h2><table><tr><th>Minute</th><th>Action and exact teaching purpose</th></tr><tr><td>0–1</td><td>State the goal: one prepared surface on the crate. Ask what should change and what should remain shared.</td></tr><tr><td>1–3</td><td>Preview changes. Read parent, texture mapping, destination and crate slot. Expect one new instance and one component assignment. The plan has made no changes.</td></tr><tr><td>3–4</td><td>Apply: create 1 instance. Read Completed and Applied change rows. Apply is disabled because the plan was consumed.</td></tr><tr><td>4–5</td><td>Preview the same name again. Ask a student to read the duplicate-name message and propose a recovery.</td></tr><tr><td>5–6</td><td>Reset practice data, retain the input name, then preview again. Distinguish reset from live Undo.</td></tr><tr><td>6–7</td><td>Ask: “Which row proves scope? What questions remain?” Expected scope: component override, not shared mesh or parent graph.</td></tr></table>
<h2>Four-minute VFX transfer</h2><p>30 seconds: state the three-marker task. 60 seconds: preview Steam, inspect transforms and 0-to-3 count, apply and inspect rows. 30 seconds: preview again and read the duplicate block. 30 seconds: reset and explain the recovery boundary. 90 seconds: questions or recovery reserve.</p><blockquote>“We reuse the same workflow with different rules. Three markers give three effects. These checks tell us about placement; they do not measure frame cost. What would we need to measure next?”</blockquote>
<h2>Fallback capture sequence</h2><p>These are actual offscreen practice captures, not live Unreal evidence.</p>'''+''.join(f'<h3>{name.replace("_"," ").title()}</h3><a href="../../../../../Week07UnrealPython/Docs/UI/captures/{name}.png"><img style="max-width:100%" src="../../../../../Week07UnrealPython/Docs/UI/captures/{name}.png" alt="{name} practice state"></a>' for name in ['material_preview','material_complete','material_blocked','vfx_preview','vfx_complete','vfx_blocked'])+'''
<h2>Optional code explanation, within the interface block</h2><p>Trace sample inputs in workflow_sample.py, plan rules/session in workflows.py, readable output in workflow_presentation.py, and UI events in ui/assistants.py. The actual Unreal adapter is editor/workflow_backend.py. Explain one connection, without opening an additional coding lesson.</p><h2>Live Unreal boundary</h2><p>Use the live route only after the project’s presentation checklist passes with real presets, assignments, placed Actors, stale selections, failure cleanup and recovery. Reset practice data does not exist in the live tool. Neither live workflow automatically saves. Component assignment Undo and cleanup of a newly created material asset are separate checks.</p><p><a href="../../../../Week07UnrealPython/Docs/UI/PRESENTATION_CHECKLIST.md">Live acceptance checklist</a> · <a href="../../../../Week07UnrealPython/Docs/DEMO_SEQUENCE.md">Current tool’s canonical demo sequence</a></p>''')
